A declaration joins a set at most once, so repeating the same directive on it is
rejected with a dedicated diagnostic, rather than silently deduped, or surfaced
as a confusing "produced by both NewT and NewT (same position)" self-collision.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
error-is: ErrDuplicateDirective
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

type T struct{}

//plumb:build
//plumb:build
func NewT() *T { return &T{} }
